WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.850
- It's very airy, and it's
kind of melts in your mouth.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.120
Hi, guys, it's Rie.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.610
Today I'm going to show you three

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.730
very different kind of cheesecake.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.670
Some of them are a little bit challenging.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.610
Don't worry, there are
some hacks that help you

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.270
make perfect cheesecake.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.970
First, Japanese souffle cheesecake.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:21.320
First, I want to prep cake pan.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.120
I'm using six inch springform pan.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:29.120
I'm going to grease my pan so
the parchment sticks better.

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.933
I'm gonna use knife to cut.

00:00:32.952 --> 00:00:34.901
(parchment ripping)

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.960
(parchment crinkling)

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.530
Springform pan come with two piece,

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:43.110
and we are going to use
water bath cooking method.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:44.980
If you put in a water,

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.990
there is a gap and water
comes into the pan,

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:51.710
so I'm going to use aluminum foil.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.250
I think springform pan
it's better for this cake

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.730
so you can easily remove from the pan.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:00.750
Now the most difficult part it's done,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:01.920
let's get to the fun part.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.400
First I'm adding cream cheese,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.530
butter, and heavy cream.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.210
We are going to use double boiler.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:13.760
So you are going to mix
until evenly smooth.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.340
I'm going to set this aside

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.410
and I'm going to separate
egg whites and egg yolk.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.160
And I'm going to add egg yolk in here.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.522
Nice color.

00:01:24.522 --> 00:01:25.355
(whisk tapping bowl)

00:01:25.355 --> 00:01:27.600
And one tablespoon of lemon juice.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.830
Usually half lemon makes
one tablespoon lemon juice.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:36.830
Now I am going to sift corn starch.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.060
I enjoy baking a lot.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.939
Of course, my favorite
part it's like eating.

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:42.772
(Rie laughing)

00:01:42.772 --> 00:01:44.450
This is already pretty smooth,

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.600
but I want to make it extra smooth,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.290
and make sure there's
no cream cheese chunks.

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.290
I'm going to put this in
the refrigerator to chill,

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:57.160
so it will incorporate
better with my meringue.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.309
I have egg whites.

00:01:59.309 --> 00:02:02.142
(beaters running)

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.690
I'm going to add sugar gradually.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:10.030
It's kinda like in between
soft peak and hard peak.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.370
So this it's the mixture I made earlier.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:18.370
I'm going to take about
1/4th of the meringue,

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.880
incorporate it well.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.180
The first mix it's done,

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.730
and I'm going to add all
the rest of the meringue.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.990
And I try not to over
mix here, but make sure

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:35.990
there is no meringue
white stream it's visible.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.320
Now I'm going to add this in a mold.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.270
Yeah, a nice ribbon.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:47.850
And I'm gonna just tap,
so there's no big bubble.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.540
I use paper towel underneath it

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.220
so doesn't give a direct heat.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.960
Pour hot water about halfway
of the springform pan.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.530
Oven temperature is a
very important factor

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.650
for this cheesecake.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.230
When I tested it cracked so many times,

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:09.570
so first we are going
to bake this lower heat.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.920
250 for 60 minutes,

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.950
increase the heat for 325
and bake for 10 minutes.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.810
Let's go to the oven.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.460
This cake it's baked.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:22.110
You want to eat right away, right,

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.560
but this cake it's taste better

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.740
if you chill in the
refrigerator at least two hours

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.470
or preferably overnight.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:30.817
I'm gonna unmold.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.330
Reveal.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:40.020
I'm brushing apricot jam,
just make the top shiny.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:43.160
And here we have it,
Japanese souffle cheesecake.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.510
Look how pretty they are.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.808
Can't wait to have a bite.

00:03:47.808 --> 00:03:49.690
(upbeat music)

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:50.890
It's really light,

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:53.740
but kinda still have like
nice cheesecake flavor,

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.930
just like taste of my childhood.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.770
And I think this is very different

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.850
and very good contrast from
the cheesecake I'm making next.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:02.683
Let's do it.

00:04:02.683 --> 00:04:04.680
We are on to the American cheesecake,

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.940
and I think the best
part, it's the bottom,

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.317
everyone is nodding here.

00:04:08.317 --> 00:04:09.160
(people laughing)

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.450
All right, so let's get started.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:15.450
First, we have 12 graham
crackers made into crumbs.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.650
One stick butter, combine well.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:23.650
All right, I'm using a
nine inch springform pan.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.244
Grease.

00:04:25.244 --> 00:04:26.077
(spraying grease)

00:04:26.077 --> 00:04:29.030
I'm going to add crumbs.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.760
Dry cup measurement, it's
a perfect things to use.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:33.863
Kind of press.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:36.773
I think that's good.

00:04:36.773 --> 00:04:39.330
So we are going to bake this at 350 degree

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:42.860
for 20 minutes and let it
cool for room temperature.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.903
I'll be right back.

00:04:45.997 --> 00:04:47.467
- [Woman] Woo, oh that was pretty good.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.450
- Now I'm going to make fillings.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.120
First I'm going to crack eggs,

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.701
and I'm going to use four eggs.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.590
(eggs cracking)

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:58.350
I have 24 ounces cream cheese.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.770
Add sugar and cream together.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:04.281
I'm going to add egg one by one.

00:05:04.281 --> 00:05:05.780
(beaters running)

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.543
I'm going to add vanilla extract.

00:05:08.594 --> 00:05:11.427
(beaters running)

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.550
Batter is ready and crust is ready.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:18.850
I'm going to use foil
technique that I showed you

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.130
for our Japanese cheesecake,
so the water doesn't get in.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.760
We are going to use water bath technique

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.700
instead of just baking in the oven,

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.140
so it's foolproof, so it won't crack.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:32.763
Now I'm going to add piece of paper towel,

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:38.870
put the pan in, and add
the batter, and shake it.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.560
And I'm going to add hot water.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.110
And we are going to bake
this at 350 for one hour,

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.470
or the center it's slightly still giggly,

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.180
but outside it's kind of set.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.463
Let's go.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.820
So I baked this cheesecake
and let it chill

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.860
for 12 hours to overnight.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.750
And I'm going to just decorate.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.530
I like decorating, I
think it's kinda nice,

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:04.740
gives a nice pop.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:08.430
I like to add mint, kinda filling the gap.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.163
Here we have it, American cheesecake.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.950
It's very rich and it's very dense.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:18.840
Nice contrast with the crust underneath.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.550
I think adding fresh fruits,

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:23.610
it gives a nice contrast
with rich cream cheese

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:24.780
to fresh fruits.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.600
This cheesecake is great, but
next one it's very exciting.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.830
The last cheesecake we are
making is basque cheesecake.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:34.540
This is known as a burnt cheesecake,

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.720
so you are going to bake
it like super high heat.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.380
And this one, it's super easy to make.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.720
I have a two pounds of cream cheese

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.163
and I'm adding sugar.

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:48.237
(beaters running)

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.770
Okay, I think this it's nice and creamy,

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:56.520
and all the sugar it's
dissolved and incorporated.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.980
I'm going to add eggs one by one.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.663
So first egg.

00:07:01.663 --> 00:07:04.496
(beaters running)

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:08.930
Scrape the side.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.550
I'm going to add two cups of heavy cream,

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:13.630
and make sure it's room temperature,

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:15.410
and I'm going to add slowly.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.250
And I'm gonna add two teaspoon of vanilla,

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.752
and one teaspoon of salt.

00:07:21.752 --> 00:07:25.040
(beaters running)

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.700
I'm going to sift flour.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.160
And if you have a stand mixer

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.660
you can totally use the stand mixer.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:32.700
(beaters running)

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.700
All right, batter it's done,

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:36.750
and I'm going to prepare my mold.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:39.050
All right so basque cheesecake hack.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:42.360
Basque cheesecake you want to
crumble the parchment paper,

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:45.070
but it's difficult to line if you crumble,

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:48.790
it kind of have a gap,
and it doesn't lying well.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:52.580
But if you soak in a
water, it's easier to line.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.416
So first we are going to crumble.

00:07:54.416 --> 00:07:55.522
(parchment crinkling)

00:07:55.522 --> 00:07:57.400
And soak in the water.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:00.070
Paper kinda become a little bit flexible.

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:01.580
A little bit moisture it's fine,

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.330
it doesn't affect anything for the cake.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.740
I'm gonna just pour.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:09.310
So I'm going to bake this at 400 degree

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.220
for 50 to 60 minutes.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:16.220
The top is dark brown and the
center part is kind of jiggly,

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:21.200
but it will set as it cooled,
so don't worry about it.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.250
Let's bake this.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.690
All right, we baked it and let it cool

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:29.110
to room temperature, and look at this.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:34.040
It is pretty dark brown,
this is what you want.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:38.030
The color is very unique
and also the texture,

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:41.430
it's the most beautiful thing
about this basque cheesecake.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:42.940
If you are beginner baker,

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:46.950
I think this it's best cheesecake
to try for the first time,

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.590
because you just mix it and
bake in high temperature.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.230
You don't need to worry about cracking,

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:53.600
'cause you want it burnt.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.800
You will gain a confidence.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.509
I like how rustic this look.

00:08:58.509 --> 00:09:00.042
Let's unmold.

00:09:00.042 --> 00:09:00.920
(parchment crinkling)

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:01.860
Ooh.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:04.773
Kinda smell like a little
bit caramelized smell.

00:09:06.135 --> 00:09:07.840
(upbeat music)

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.880
Mm, so different, unreal.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.680
So it kinda like s'more.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.940
You want to burn marshmallow, right.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:17.100
I made three different cheese cake today.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.760
Japanese souffle cheesecake,

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:21.500
American cheesecake,
and basque cheesecake.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.850
I hope you guys enjoy watching this video.

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:25.720
If you make any of those cheesecake,

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:28.460
tag me on Instagram,
and see you next time.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:30.350
Thank you for watching.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.672
- [Man] Oh, yes.

00:09:31.672 --> 00:09:34.255
(upbeat music)

